			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"The Hoarfrost called it the Held Beast, and held is the word they used for prisoners."
				"It was never sealed inside anything. It was bound to the mountain and left free within it,"
				"which the Convent files under substrate-held, the same class as a god bound to its own sleep."
				"The keepers kept a vigil and the rule of the vigil was that nobody engage it. Their whole"
				"preservation-architecture rested on it not waking. When the Hoarfrost fell around CR 600 the"
				"vigil ended with them. It still sleeps. Not because anyone is still watching."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			icon: {
